            <ArticleTitle>Microbial separation from a complex matrix by a hand-held microfluidic device.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10788-10791</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc06310e</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Through a simple chemical activation of biomolecules present in the outer structures of microbial cells, microorganisms can be rapidly isolated on gold-coated surfaces in a microfluidic device with over 99% capture efficiency. Bacterial and fungal cells can be selectively captured, concentrated and retrieved for further analysis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
